# Allowlist. The context is the repo root (6.7 GB); this cuts it to 56 kB,
# which is everything Bundler needs to resolve the bundle and nothing else.
#
# A denylist was rejected: it makes every new large directory in the repo a
# silent context regression, and the k8s/docker equivalent is 486 lines.
#
# Re-including a nested path needs its parents un-excluded, hence the
# dashboard two-step: allow the directory, drop its contents, allow engines.
# Only the gemspecs and their version.rb are let through, matching the COPY
# lines in the Dockerfile — engine source would only invalidate the bundle.
#
# Verified on docker, on podman 5.8/buildah 1.43, and on the buildah 1.33.7
# floor: all three honor the <dockerfile>.dockerignore convention and fail
# the build when an excluded path is COPYed. buildah names the file in the
# error, which is how the negative test confirms it rather than guessing.
*
!.ruby-version
!Gemfile
!Gemfile.lock
!dashboard
dashboard/*
!dashboard/engines
dashboard/engines/*/*
!dashboard/engines/*/*.gemspec
!dashboard/engines/*/lib
dashboard/engines/*/lib/*
!dashboard/engines/*/lib/*/version.rb
